A continuation paragraph belongs to the item above it, so a task list of
two items with a continuation is TWO items and not three, and the block
covers the continuation.

`format` can only show what the writer does. This case reads the block
model instead, which is what every edit by index depends on: `insert-after`,
`replace` and `remove` all count blocks and items. If the continuation were
split off as an item of its own, the count here would say three and every
later edit would land one item out.

The line range matters as much as the count. L3-7 reaches the last line of
the second item, so the continuation is inside the block rather than after
it.
